    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "We analyze the LCT attack on a noised pseudorandom sequence generator involving a primitive known as The Binary Rate Multiplier (BRM). BRM consists of 2 linear feedback shift registers (LFSRs). One of them, the clocking LFSR (LFSRs), determines the clocking sequence for the clocked LFSR (LFSRu), see Fig. 1."
